      "reasons": [
        "The packet does not define “supported living” as “a housing arrangement where a person lives in accommodation that includes some ongoing support or supervision.” It only mentions that, in Sweden, mentally disordered offenders often reside in “supported living accommodations post-discharge from forensic psychiatric services.”",
        "The definition’s claim that, in this context, help with medication administration may matter is only partially supported: the packet supports that “stability of living arrangement” and “supervision of pharmacological administration” are among the social/environmental factors associated with medication discontinuation, but it does not explicitly connect these points as “help with medication administration” within a definitional description of supported living."
